            <ArticleTitle>Similarities between interstitial cystitis/bladder pain syndrome and vulvodynia: implications for patient management.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>643-52</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.3978/j.issn.2223-4683.2015.10.09</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Interstitial cystitis/bladder pain syndrome (IC/BPS) and vulvodynia are chronic pain syndromes that appear to be intertwined from the perspectives of embryology, pathology and epidemiology. These associations may account for similar responses to various therapies.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
